Skip v_wait's idle passes on the host while native 60 has the clock raised.

Measured in play with 0033 and 0034 in: every frame fitted one field (100%),
but in busy scenes (1,200-2,100 prims) the emulation thread spent 980-990 ms of
each second emulating and 0 ms idle, VBlank fell to 42-59/s and speed to
0.87-0.94. The guest had finished its frame; the host was spending the rest of
the field executing PsyQ's v_wait - 14 instructions, three RAM loads and a
store per pass - one pass at a time, twice as many per field at 200%.

The runtime's generic wait-loop skip does not apply: it is opt-in, and its
first gate is "no guest stores", while v_wait stores its timeout counter to
the stack every pass. This adds a skip specific to that loop, in
crash2_60fps.h, on the same rule as the generic one:

  - At the loop head (0x8004A5F4, the back-edge's check PC) measure passes:
    same sp, same target, counter down by exactly one, gap under 512 cycles.
  - After four clean passes, skip whole passes up to two short of the next
    DELIVERABLE interrupt (psx_cycles_to_next_idle_event - the generic skip's
    own bound, now exported from psx_cycles.c), costed at the measured
    average; decrement the stack counter by the passes skipped. Real passes
    then cross the event, so the interrupt is taken where it would have been,
    give or take one pass.
  - Never when an unmasked interrupt is already pending: the generic skip
    runs inside the interrupt check before deliverability is evaluated, this
    runs just after it, so it tests that itself.
  - Never leaves the counter below 2, so the game's own timeout path stays
    reachable.
  - Only with the mode on, the gate open, the clock above 100 and the
    revision verified; the loop's words are added to c2_60_signature_ok.
    Excluded under netplay, self-check, replay and exception handling, like
    the generic skip. PSX_CRASH2_VWAIT_SKIP=0 disables it for A/B.

Heartbeat gains native_60fps_vwait_skipped (cumulative guest cycles). Its rate
over the guest clock is the spin the host no longer runs.

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake.

