+ * emulation thread spent 980-990 ms of every second emulating and 0 ms idle,
+ * VBlank fell to 42-59/s and the whole machine ran at 0.87-0.94 speed, while
+ * 100% of frames still fitted a field. The guest was done; the host was busy
+ * spinning on its behalf.
+ *
+ * The runtime has a generic wait-loop skip, but its first gate is "no guest
+ * stores", and v_wait stores its timeout counter to the stack every pass. So
+ * this one is specific to this loop, verified word for word by
+ * c2_60_signature_ok, and follows the same rule as the generic one: skip whole
+ * passes, and stop short of the next DELIVERABLE interrupt
+ * (psx_cycles_to_next_idle_event, the bound the generic skip uses). A loop
+ * that only reads RAM cannot see anything change until an interrupt is taken,
+ * so every pass skipped is one it would have spent reading the same values.
+ *
+ * It stops C2_60_VW_MARGIN passes short, so real passes cross the event and
+ * the interrupt is taken where it would have been, give or take one pass. The
+ * stack counter is decremented by the passes skipped and never allowed near
+ * -1, so the game's own timeout path stays reachable. Active only while this
+ * mode has the clock raised; PSX_CRASH2_VWAIT_SKIP=0 turns it off for A/B. */
